WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.150
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:03.420 --> 00:04.546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

3
00:04.630 --> 00:05.923
START DATING...

4
00:36.620 --> 00:40.958
BETWEEN STEPS

5
00:41.583 --> 00:43.835
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

6
00:43.919 --> 00:45.546
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

7
00:46.547 --> 00:48.799
EPISODE 2

8
01:18.870 --> 01:20.831
What are you doing up so late?

9
01:20.914 --> 01:22.416
What time is it now?

10
01:23.417 --> 01:25.919
[Miyoung] What are you still doing up at this hour? Huh?

11
01:26.503 --> 01:27.504
Something like this.

12
01:28.338 --> 01:31.216
What... What's all this? Huh?

13
01:31.300 --> 01:32.342
[Youjin] Cool, isn't it?

14
01:32.926 --> 01:35.846
So now you want to be a cartoonist instead of a designer?

15
01:36.513 --> 01:39.600
No, your daughter is going to get her PhD now.

16
01:40.100 --> 01:41.810
-Thank you. -Goodbye.

17
01:45.731 --> 01:46.815
Huh?

18
01:48.025 --> 01:51.320
Oh, Minjae. I want the expensive coffee too.

19
01:52.487 --> 01:54.740
I'm sorry, but could I get a refund?

20
01:54.823 --> 01:56.116
-You'd like a refund? -Yes.

21
01:56.199 --> 01:57.534
Please insert your card.

22
02:15.802 --> 02:18.055
[Youjin] I double-majored in fashion and mathematics.

23
02:18.138 --> 02:20.432
So I've completed all the required coursework.

24
02:21.058 --> 02:22.976
My grades aren't that bad, either.

25
02:26.229 --> 02:27.689
I scored over 500 on the TEPS too.

26
02:29.650 --> 02:32.903
But why do you suddenly want to switch to a completely different major?

27
02:32.986 --> 02:34.321
Uh...

28
02:34.404 --> 02:36.990
I've always liked tinkering with machines.

29
02:37.074 --> 02:39.660
I was good at building things with LEGOs too.

30
02:39.743 --> 02:41.995
I even won an award for it as a kid.

31
02:42.079 --> 02:43.205
LEGOs?

32
02:46.083 --> 02:47.668
Yeah. And I can code too.

33
02:47.751 --> 02:48.919
Oh?

34
02:49.711 --> 02:54.257
Then do you know how to use MATLAB or SolidWorks too?

35
02:54.841 --> 02:57.386
No. What are those?

36
02:58.720 --> 02:59.971
You don't.

37
03:00.681 --> 03:02.432
I don't know what they are...

38
03:04.351 --> 03:05.602
but I can learn.

39
03:06.186 --> 03:10.023
I'm a fast learner. And once I start something, I go all out.

40
03:13.151 --> 03:16.405
I have never written a mechanical engineering research proposal before.

41
03:16.488 --> 03:17.823
So if you could take a look...

42
03:17.906 --> 03:18.907
But...

43
03:21.201 --> 03:25.622
if you like machines and you're good at building with LEGOs,

44
03:26.623 --> 03:27.624
they can be your hobbies.

45
03:27.707 --> 03:29.251
Why go so far as to switch majors?

46
03:31.628 --> 03:33.046
Well, that's because I...

47
03:35.882 --> 03:38.093
Fashion and textiles just wasn't for me.

48
03:39.970 --> 03:43.265
It turns out I don't have any talent for it.

49
03:46.393 --> 03:48.395
"It turns out"?

50
03:50.397 --> 03:52.858
But what about all you've learned? What a waste.

51
03:53.442 --> 03:56.987
All the time and money over the past four years will go to waste.

52
03:58.405 --> 04:00.699
And what if you get into grad school,

53
04:01.450 --> 04:05.370
and it turns out that you don't have any talent

54
04:06.538 --> 04:08.123
for mechanical engineering?

55
04:08.206 --> 04:10.375
Are you going to switch to business then?

56
04:19.509 --> 04:22.345
[muttering] Look at you, so smart. What are you, judge and jury?

57
04:23.138 --> 04:24.139
[Minjae] Pardon?

58
04:26.016 --> 04:27.100
[Youjin] I mean,

59
04:27.601 --> 04:31.062
maybe you should've gone to law school instead of engineering school.

60
04:31.146 --> 04:33.523
Just a random thought.

61
04:36.109 --> 04:37.360
What I'm saying is,

62
04:37.444 --> 04:41.448
switching majors isn't something you should decide on rashly like that.

63
04:42.240 --> 04:44.075
First, everything you learned is wasted.

64
04:44.159 --> 04:46.578
Plus, won't you feel guilty toward your parents?

65
04:48.830 --> 04:52.584
Anyway, you've still got some time, so take your time and think it over.

66
04:56.880 --> 04:57.881
Are you angry?

67
04:59.090 --> 05:00.592
No, I'm not angry.

68
05:00.675 --> 05:01.843
I think you're angry.

69
05:01.927 --> 05:04.554
I don't get angry so easily.

70
05:15.899 --> 05:16.900
What is it?

71
05:18.485 --> 05:19.486
What?

72
05:20.403 --> 05:21.404
It's nothing.

73
05:23.532 --> 05:25.617
[Hangyeol] He was sitting side by side with a woman,

74
05:25.700 --> 05:28.662
looking at something on a laptop.

75
05:28.745 --> 05:30.831
Was she pretty? Was she a pretty woman?

76
05:30.914 --> 05:32.332
[Hangyeol] She was gorgeous.

77
05:32.415 --> 05:34.668
Is she in our program? One of the younger students?

78
05:34.751 --> 05:38.171
No, she's not in our program. She's some woman I don't know.

79
05:38.880 --> 05:42.759
He was looking at something on a laptop with some pretty woman you don't know?

80
05:42.843 --> 05:44.261
Sitting side by side?

81
05:44.761 --> 05:46.763
How pretty? As pretty as aespa? IVE?

82
05:46.847 --> 05:49.057
No, not like that.

83
05:50.016 --> 05:52.978
You know, that American model.

84
05:53.061 --> 05:54.437
Which American model?

85
05:55.105 --> 05:57.399
I can't remember her name all of a sudden.

86
05:57.482 --> 06:00.151
She's really beautiful and has a baby face.

87
06:00.235 --> 06:02.070
She's been married three times.

88
06:02.696 --> 06:04.531
She's been married three times?

89
06:05.115 --> 06:06.700
That's how pretty she is.

90
06:06.783 --> 06:09.452
Beautiful women get three, four chances at marriage.

91
06:09.536 --> 06:12.122
For women like that, it's polyandry, not polygyny.

92
06:12.205 --> 06:14.457
All right, hold on. I'll just ask.

93
06:14.541 --> 06:15.542
[Hangyeol] Ask who?

94
06:15.625 --> 06:17.586
-Chacha. -[line ringing]

95
06:17.669 --> 06:20.797
[hesitating] Hey, Seohyun, you picked up fast. Are you busy?

96
06:20.881 --> 06:24.259
I just wanted to ask you something. Yeah.

97
06:24.342 --> 06:28.763
So, Hangyeol saw Minjae with some woman.

98
06:28.847 --> 06:31.766
Uh-huh. No. She's not a student in our program.

99
06:31.850 --> 06:36.104
Anyway, he says she's really pretty and baby-faced

100
06:36.187 --> 06:38.565
and looks like an American model, yeah.

101
06:38.648 --> 06:40.859
Is that Seohyun? Do you think she would know?

102
06:43.862 --> 06:46.072
Oh, you saw her too?

103
06:46.156 --> 06:47.657
She saw her? She says she did?

104
06:47.741 --> 06:50.035
See? I said I saw her. I really saw her. Seriously...

105
06:50.118 --> 06:54.331
[Taeho] Seohyun. So who is she? Yeah, she's not in our program.

106
06:54.414 --> 06:56.291
-[door opens] -[whispers] He's here.

107
06:57.375 --> 06:58.376
Hey.

108
07:04.049 --> 07:06.801
What's with the weird vibe here?

109
07:12.724 --> 07:15.477
Okay, so this is the load torque on the knee,

110
07:15.560 --> 07:17.062
and this is the friction torque.

111
07:17.145 --> 07:18.647
DANNY WALKING MODEL VALIDATION

112
07:18.730 --> 07:22.275
The little bits of friction generated in the gears and the belt

113
07:22.359 --> 07:23.360
are hard to notice,

114
07:23.443 --> 07:25.445
but they play a bigger role than you'd think.

115
07:25.528 --> 07:28.573
But we only factored the load torque into the simulation.

116
07:28.657 --> 07:31.159
So the robot seemed to walk fine at first.

117
07:31.242 --> 07:34.621
But on the actual robot, the friction torque acts on it too,

118
07:34.704 --> 07:38.416
so the knee hesitates a little before it starts moving.

119
07:40.794 --> 07:43.004
It's about time I sent you to Dieland, isn't it?

120
07:43.088 --> 07:44.089
Focus, will you?

121
07:44.172 --> 07:45.256
I...

122
07:46.633 --> 07:48.551
I honestly thought... [clears throat]

123
07:48.635 --> 07:50.970
...of you as my soulmate,

124
07:51.054 --> 07:52.055
until now.

125
07:53.640 --> 07:57.227
Your soulmate is your girlfriend, who is in Daejeon now.

126
07:57.310 --> 07:58.311
[Taeho] Minjae,

127
07:58.395 --> 08:03.942
I truly thought of you as my own brother, you know?

128
08:04.442 --> 08:06.277
But... [sighs]

129
08:07.237 --> 08:10.198
...how come I didn't know something even Chacha knew?

130
08:10.281 --> 08:12.033
That really hurt my feelings.

131
08:12.117 --> 08:13.118
The thing is...

132
08:14.369 --> 08:15.453
there's nothing.

133
08:15.537 --> 08:17.247
I have nothing to tell you.

134
08:17.330 --> 08:19.082
Stop it and just be honest with me.

135
08:19.165 --> 08:20.625
What do you mean, be honest?

136
08:21.126 --> 08:23.461
-[Taeho sighs] -Are you dating that woman?

137
08:23.545 --> 08:25.797
No, there's nothing going on between us.

138
08:25.880 --> 08:29.509
I saw the two of you sitting side by side, watching a movie and giggling.

139
08:30.093 --> 08:32.721
I wasn't giggling, I wasn't watching a movie,

140
08:32.804 --> 08:34.139
and there's nothing going on.

141
08:34.222 --> 08:36.891
-I've said it three times now. -[Taeho] Then prove it.

142
08:37.392 --> 08:38.476
Prove what, and how?

143
08:39.060 --> 08:42.397
If there's really nothing between you two and you're being honest, then...

144
08:43.148 --> 08:44.441
set Hangyeol up with her.

145
08:45.900 --> 08:47.110
-What? -Yeah.

146
08:48.194 --> 08:49.612
Set me up with her.

147
08:49.696 --> 08:51.656
[Taeho] He's really into her.

148
08:52.407 --> 08:53.908
Yeah, she's so beautiful.

149
08:54.701 --> 08:57.203
I like her. Set me up with her.

150
08:57.287 --> 09:00.707
Dude, respect the pecking order. He has to set me up first.

151
09:00.790 --> 09:04.210
You didn't even get a look at her. Why would you be set up with her?

152
09:04.294 --> 09:05.712
[Minjae tapping on board] That's enough.

153
09:05.795 --> 09:07.881
Stop talking nonsense. Where were we?

154
09:08.423 --> 09:13.094
Right, anyway, now we need to incorporate this friction model into the simulation.

155
09:13.178 --> 09:14.179
[Hangyeol] If...

156
09:15.972 --> 09:20.226
If you don't set me up on a date, I'm going to quit the lab.

157
09:20.727 --> 09:21.728
What?

158
09:22.896 --> 09:27.233
I'll also quit the lab if you don't set me up on a date.

159
09:29.319 --> 09:30.695
Well done, guys.

160
09:31.446 --> 09:33.865
[sighs] Fine, quit then. Just quit. Go on and quit.

161
09:33.948 --> 09:34.991
Quit the lab.

162
09:35.075 --> 09:38.745
I'll talk to the professor, so you two bring me your withdrawal forms.

163
09:38.828 --> 09:42.791
[chuckles] Right, Chansoo, you got an offer from KAIST, right?

164
09:42.874 --> 09:43.875
-Yes. -Yeah.

165
09:43.958 --> 09:46.252
Professor Hwang Semin's lab reached out to me.

166
09:46.336 --> 09:48.671
They asked if I'd join them for the upcoming WRS.

167
09:50.006 --> 09:53.885
KAIST is preparing for the WRS? But they didn't participate last year.

168
09:53.968 --> 09:55.595
Not sure, but they are this year.

169
09:55.678 --> 09:56.679
Is that so?

170
09:57.597 --> 09:58.932
[Hangyeol] What's the WRS?

171
09:59.474 --> 10:01.684
-[groans] -[in English] World Robot Summit.

172
10:05.313 --> 10:07.398
[in Korean] Are you setting me up on a date or not?

173
10:22.247 --> 10:23.748
See? She's not answering.

174
10:23.832 --> 10:25.500
-She will. -[line connects]

175
10:25.583 --> 10:26.668
[Youjin on phone] Hello?

176
10:27.168 --> 10:28.169
Hello?

177
10:29.963 --> 10:32.173
Ah, I wasn't doing anything.

178
10:33.299 --> 10:35.969
There's a book I need to read, so I was reading that.

179
10:36.052 --> 10:39.931
Oh. It's nothing serious. I just wanted to ask you something.

180
10:42.392 --> 10:43.685
Sure, go ahead and ask.

181
10:47.814 --> 10:49.107
Boyfriend?

182
10:51.109 --> 10:54.279
But why do you want to know that?

183
10:55.822 --> 10:58.950
[chuckles] Why do you care if I have a boyfriend or not...

184
11:00.660 --> 11:03.079
No. I don't have a boyfriend.

185
11:03.663 --> 11:06.499
-Why do you ask? -[digital door lock beeping]

186
11:10.253 --> 11:11.588
Hey, why are you home today?

187
11:12.380 --> 11:17.135
[Youjin] I can't really talk right now. Can we talk later? Yes.

188
11:18.052 --> 11:20.013
-[grunts] -Yes.

189
11:22.015 --> 11:24.934
Mom. Lim Youjin is seeing someone.

190
11:32.483 --> 11:34.736
You're seeing someone these days, aren't you?

191
11:35.987 --> 11:36.988
No, I'm not.

192
11:37.739 --> 11:39.324
Then why did you hide earlier?

193
11:40.158 --> 11:43.411
What do you mean, hide? I just wanted to talk somewhere quiet.

194
11:44.954 --> 11:46.664
[Miyoung] Are you really not seeing anyone?

195
11:47.165 --> 11:50.627
No. I'm way too busy studying, you know.

196
11:50.710 --> 11:53.838
I barely get any sleep as it is. How would I even have time to date?

197
11:53.922 --> 11:58.134
Exactly. You're in the prime of your life, and all you do is sit at that desk.

198
11:58.718 --> 12:00.345
Aren't you going to get married?

199
12:01.137 --> 12:03.014
I'm never getting married.

200
12:03.097 --> 12:04.891
I'm going to live with you forever.

201
12:04.974 --> 12:08.019
You can't do that. You have to get married, still.

202
12:09.479 --> 12:10.813
Dad, do you believe that?

203
12:11.898 --> 12:13.566
The three biggest lies in Korea

204
12:13.650 --> 12:15.777
are old folks saying, "I should just die already,"

205
12:15.860 --> 12:19.447
and daughters saying, "I'm going to live with Mom and Dad forever."

206
12:20.615 --> 12:22.617
What was the last one? There are three of them.

207
12:22.700 --> 12:24.786
They're not lies. They're just trying to be nice.

208
12:26.079 --> 12:28.498
See? This is why daughters are different from sons.

209
12:29.499 --> 12:31.376
This is why it's nice to have a daughter.

210
12:31.459 --> 12:32.710
-Mmm-hmm. -[Miyoung] Yeah.

211
12:32.794 --> 12:36.923
What? What's wrong with sons? Why are you playing favorites?

212
12:37.006 --> 12:38.675
When did I play favorites?

213
12:38.758 --> 12:40.260
Just now.

214
12:41.010 --> 12:43.096
Lim Youjin is always right, isn't she?

215
12:43.930 --> 12:47.684
Even if she told you doenjang was made from red beans,

216
12:47.767 --> 12:49.018
you'd believe her, right?

217
12:49.102 --> 12:50.103
Yes.

218
12:50.812 --> 12:53.940
It's meju, not doenjang. It's "Meju is made from red beans."

219
12:55.108 --> 12:56.901
It's meju? Hmm.

220
13:00.196 --> 13:02.198
So you're not seeing anyone?

221
13:02.782 --> 13:03.992
Mmm.

222
13:04.075 --> 13:05.451
I don't have time for it.

223
13:05.535 --> 13:09.038
I mean, it's okay if you date. It's okay.

224
13:10.081 --> 13:11.749
Just let me meet the guy first.

225
13:13.001 --> 13:14.043
Okay.

226
13:15.503 --> 13:17.130
I don't ask for much.

227
13:17.797 --> 13:19.424
Just someone who's hardworking,

228
13:21.342 --> 13:25.179
respects his elders, and is healthy, with all four limbs intact.

229
13:25.263 --> 13:28.099
Other than that, I don't ask for anything.

230
13:29.058 --> 13:31.311
[Miyoung] What do you mean, all four limbs?

231
13:31.394 --> 13:33.104
Who doesn't have four limbs?

232
13:33.187 --> 13:34.897
-[chuckles] -[Yongseok] Some people don't.

233
13:34.981 --> 13:36.232
You know, people with disabilities.

234
13:36.733 --> 13:38.401
-[Miyoung] You little... -Come on.

235
13:38.901 --> 13:39.944
[Miyoung] No more food for you.

236
15:03.152 --> 15:07.573
If you keep pulling all-nighters, your skin's going to become dull.

237
15:09.242 --> 15:12.245
I know. It'll get all dry, right?

238
15:13.037 --> 15:14.372
What am I going to do?

239
15:16.249 --> 15:17.917
Are you really not seeing anyone?

240
15:19.127 --> 15:22.046
No. Lim Youseong got it totally wrong.

241
15:22.130 --> 15:23.131
Hmm.

242
15:24.257 --> 15:26.968
I'm actually more worried about your love life

243
15:27.051 --> 15:29.053
than your grad school entrance exam.

244
15:31.639 --> 15:33.683
Do you want me to set you up with someone?

245
15:34.475 --> 15:38.896
One of our customers at the auto shop owns a huge building near Gangnam Station.

246
15:40.189 --> 15:42.275
I said you go to Seohan National University,

247
15:42.358 --> 15:44.318
and they asked to see a picture of you.

248
15:45.027 --> 15:47.530
So I showed them one, and they said,

249
15:47.613 --> 15:50.700
"She's this pretty, and she's smart too?"

250
15:51.450 --> 15:53.369
They'd love you as a daughter-in-law.

251
15:54.787 --> 15:57.331
Guess their son didn't do too well in school.

252
15:57.415 --> 16:02.044
I didn't ask. Well, I don't even need to ask.

253
16:02.128 --> 16:05.173
Any school that's not Harvard is below Seohan anyway.

254
16:08.759 --> 16:10.511
Yeah, never mind. [clears throat]

255
16:11.179 --> 16:12.263
He's no good.

256
16:12.972 --> 16:16.601
You need a man who's smart. A dumb guy won't do.

257
16:18.436 --> 16:19.812
[Youjin] Yeah.

258
16:19.896 --> 16:23.733
He has to be handsome and tall.

259
16:25.234 --> 16:26.235
[Youjin] Yeah.

260
16:27.278 --> 16:28.362
A woman

261
16:29.363 --> 16:32.450
should always be with a man who loves her

262
16:33.367 --> 16:35.328
more than she loves him.

263
16:35.411 --> 16:37.914
He's smart, handsome, and tall.

264
16:38.789 --> 16:41.209
What if he doesn't like me? That could happen.

265
16:42.543 --> 16:44.629
That's just not possible.

266
16:45.463 --> 16:47.882
I'm not saying this because you're my daughter.

267
16:47.965 --> 16:50.885
You're really cool and attractive.

268
16:52.053 --> 16:56.474
But I'm not some goddess, like Venus. I may not be everyone's type.

269
16:58.935 --> 17:00.937
Type isn't the issue with you.

270
17:01.979 --> 17:04.148
Any guy who doesn't like you is an idiot.

271
17:05.983 --> 17:08.736
Don't date someone like that.

272
17:11.572 --> 17:14.992
But what if I like the idiot anyway?

273
17:15.952 --> 17:18.162
You can't always control how you feel, right?

274
17:21.207 --> 17:22.208
Hmm?

275
17:40.851 --> 17:41.852
No.

276
17:48.859 --> 17:49.860
Hmm.

277
17:59.537 --> 18:02.456
At least get the dirt and sand off for now.

278
18:03.708 --> 18:04.709
I'm okay.

279
18:04.792 --> 18:06.127
No, hurry and wipe it off.

280
18:06.210 --> 18:10.214
If not cleaned right away, it could lead to ulcers and infection.

281
18:49.295 --> 18:50.504
Hey.

282
18:51.797 --> 18:52.798
You're here.

283
18:56.802 --> 18:58.346
What the... You guys came together?

284
19:01.265 --> 19:02.475
-Come on. Have a seat. -Hmm?

285
19:06.103 --> 19:07.104
[Minjae] Hmm.

286
19:07.188 --> 19:10.107
So, this is Lim Youjin.

287
19:11.192 --> 19:15.696
And this is Chansoo. We work in the same lab. Bae Chansoo.

288
19:16.822 --> 19:18.491
-Hello. -Hello.

289
19:18.574 --> 19:21.452
I've heard so much about you. You're really beautiful.

290
19:24.497 --> 19:26.624
-Here's the menu. -[Minjae] Thank you.

291
19:26.707 --> 19:28.084
Why don't we order first?

292
19:29.919 --> 19:31.337
Everything's good here.

293
19:31.420 --> 19:34.215
The creamy shrimp pasta is great, and so is the risotto.

294
19:37.134 --> 19:38.511
There are more in the back.

295
19:38.594 --> 19:41.222
Here. Soup. Appetizers.

296
19:42.139 --> 19:43.474
Order everything you want.

297
19:44.392 --> 19:47.436
Yes. Go ahead and order everything you want. It's on me.

298
19:48.813 --> 19:49.814
Okay.

299
19:50.481 --> 19:54.026
Then I'll just get the creamy shrimp pasta.

300
19:54.110 --> 19:56.237
The creamy shrimp pasta. And you, Chansoo?

301
19:56.320 --> 19:58.447
Then I'll get the creamy shrimp pasta too.

302
19:58.531 --> 20:00.700
Two creamy shrimp pastas.

303
20:00.783 --> 20:03.786
-Excuse me, we'd like to order. -[server] Yes.

304
20:04.995 --> 20:07.039
Could we have two orders of creamy shrimp pasta, please?

305
20:07.123 --> 20:09.208
-All right. Thank you. -Yes, thank you.

306
20:18.843 --> 20:19.844
Right.

307
20:20.344 --> 20:23.764
I've got some more work to do back at the lab, so I'll get going.

308
20:23.848 --> 20:25.975
Enjoy your meal, and get to know each other.

309
20:26.058 --> 20:27.810
Your matchmaker will leave you to it.

310
20:40.698 --> 20:41.699
-Hmm. -[bell tinkles]

311
20:55.171 --> 20:58.215
Actually, I haven't been on many blind dates,

312
20:58.299 --> 20:59.884
so this feels a little awkward.

313
21:00.718 --> 21:01.719
[Youjin] Hmm.

314
21:01.802 --> 21:05.556
I didn't know this was a blind date.

315
21:10.686 --> 21:13.481
You didn't know about this? You didn't know?

316
21:14.482 --> 21:19.320
No, I did hear it's a blind date. I did hear about it, but...

317
21:21.322 --> 21:24.742
Sometimes, I get the wrong idea in my head, and I get tunnel vision.

318
21:25.534 --> 21:27.536
I can be a real idiot sometimes.

319
21:31.791 --> 21:32.958
I see.

320
21:33.501 --> 21:34.752
-Yeah. -[bell tinkles]

321
21:44.512 --> 21:46.263
Excuse me, are you Mr. Bae Chansoo?

322
21:47.431 --> 21:49.600
Oh, you are. I was right.

323
21:50.392 --> 21:53.896
I was just walking by and thought it was you.

324
21:56.148 --> 22:00.069
Hello. I work with Chansoo in the lab.

325
22:00.152 --> 22:01.737
I'm Choi Hangyeol.

326
22:01.821 --> 22:02.822
[Youjin] Oh...

327
22:05.032 --> 22:08.452
I'm not interrupting anything, am I?

328
22:08.953 --> 22:10.412
[Youjin] No, not at all.

329
22:11.497 --> 22:14.291
I mean, what a coincidence, running into him here.

330
22:14.375 --> 22:17.711
I'm just so happy to see him. What should I do now?

331
22:18.379 --> 22:22.258
Do you mind if I join you for a bit? Just for a moment.

332
22:22.341 --> 22:24.677
-Sure, it's okay. Please have a seat here. -Oh.

333
22:32.935 --> 22:34.937
[whispering] Dude, what are you doing here?

334
22:35.020 --> 22:36.522
[whispering] It's okay.

335
22:38.190 --> 22:41.068
I haven't eaten yet, actually.

336
22:41.151 --> 22:42.361
Can I order something too?

337
22:42.444 --> 22:45.364
Yes, of course. If you haven't eaten yet...

338
22:45.990 --> 22:47.658
-Excuse me. -[server] Yes.

339
22:47.741 --> 22:48.909
[Youjin] We'd like to order.

340
22:48.993 --> 22:50.786
[whispering] What on earth are you doing here?

341
22:52.037 --> 22:55.791
[softly] I saw her first. I deserve a chance too.

342
22:57.209 --> 22:58.252
-Water? -[Hangyeol] Oh.

343
23:08.804 --> 23:11.181
Is that Chansoo and Hangyeol, by any chance?

344
23:11.682 --> 23:14.560
Ah, it is. [laughs awkwardly]

345
23:15.311 --> 23:18.230
Hello. What a coincidence.

346
23:21.442 --> 23:23.110
Funny running into you like this.

347
23:27.323 --> 23:28.699
Hello.

348
23:28.782 --> 23:33.412
I'm lab mates with them.

349
23:33.495 --> 23:35.080
-[Youjin] Hmm. -[chuckling]

350
23:35.706 --> 23:38.709
-[Hangyeol chuckles awkwardly] -Man. How funny is this? [laughing]

351
23:40.711 --> 23:43.714
-[Hangyeol] So, would you like some pasta? -Yeah, I'd love that.

352
23:50.429 --> 23:52.097
-Yes, come in. -[door opens]

353
23:55.935 --> 23:58.312
Is this Professor Ahn Jaehong's lab?

354
23:58.395 --> 24:00.940
Yes, this is Professor Ahn's lab. And who are you?

355
24:05.319 --> 24:06.320
Uh...

356
24:06.403 --> 24:10.407
Hello. I'm Kim Sejin. I study electronic engineering at KAIST.

357
24:10.491 --> 24:14.370
KAIST electronic... Right. I got your email. Come on in.

358
24:14.453 --> 24:15.454
Man.

359
24:15.537 --> 24:17.122
So everyone misunderstood.

360
24:17.206 --> 24:18.207
Yeah.

361
24:19.583 --> 24:22.294
But really, there's absolutely nothing going on between us.

362
24:22.378 --> 24:25.965
Mr. Park Minjae and I just know each other's names and faces.

363
24:26.048 --> 24:27.049
[Taeho] Hmm.

364
24:27.841 --> 24:32.096
Park Minjae isn't exactly my type, either. I can't stand guys like him.

365
24:34.223 --> 24:36.850
I was just asking him for some advice

366
24:36.934 --> 24:39.812
about applying to grad school that day.

367
24:41.689 --> 24:44.191
Grad school? Our program?

368
24:44.274 --> 24:48.529
I double-majored in fashion and textiles and mathematics.

369
24:48.612 --> 24:51.490
I've taken the required courses, and my grades aren't bad.

370
24:51.573 --> 24:52.825
And I scored over 500 on TEPS.

371
24:54.785 --> 24:58.080
Have you always been interested in mechanical engineering?

372
24:58.163 --> 25:00.582
Yes, I've always liked tinkering with machines.

373
25:01.709 --> 25:04.211
I won first prize in a LEGO-building contest once.

374
25:04.294 --> 25:06.088
I can code too.

375
25:09.633 --> 25:11.510
[Hangyeol] Anything involving robots?

376
25:12.803 --> 25:15.389
We're a robotics lab.

377
25:17.141 --> 25:20.394
Our professor is really great.

378
25:20.477 --> 25:21.478
[Hangyeol] Yeah.

379
25:21.562 --> 25:24.690
There are also scholarships available, and the stipend's pretty good too.

380
25:24.773 --> 25:25.899
It's honestly a great lab.

381
25:26.608 --> 25:30.946
Have you reached out to any other labs?

382
25:31.030 --> 25:32.614
No, not yet.

383
25:32.698 --> 25:35.325
I don't even know if I can get in or not.

384
25:35.409 --> 25:38.871
But with grades like yours, of course you'd get in.

385
25:38.954 --> 25:41.540
Do you know how hard it is to find lab slaves these days?

386
25:43.751 --> 25:48.714
Actually, I'm basically the one

387
25:48.797 --> 25:52.384
who chooses the students for our lab.

388
25:53.594 --> 25:56.221
You should see the Robot Control Room while you're here.

389
25:56.305 --> 25:57.639
It's right around the corner.

390
25:57.723 --> 25:58.724
Okay.

391
25:59.933 --> 26:04.104
Right, I heard you've completed the URP at KAIST.

392
26:04.188 --> 26:05.522
[Sejin] Yes.

393
26:05.606 --> 26:09.276
[Minjae] May I ask why you reached out to us instead of their lab?

394
26:10.611 --> 26:14.031
[Sejin] I read Professor Ahn's works. His research seems like a good fit.

395
26:14.531 --> 26:17.659
I also heard his lab is basically a free-range lab.

396
26:17.743 --> 26:20.746
Our reputation made it to your school?

397
26:20.829 --> 26:21.997
-[Sejin] Yeah. -[Minjae exclaims]

398
26:22.498 --> 26:23.499
[Minjae] After you.

399
26:25.584 --> 26:27.086
-[groans softly] -Yes.

400
26:28.712 --> 26:31.799
Well, uh, our lab is pretty hands-off.

401
26:32.549 --> 26:36.428
Professor Ahn values student autonomy over short-term results,

402
26:36.512 --> 26:39.056
which is how we got the whole free-range reputation...

403
26:39.556 --> 26:41.016
I didn't mean that in a bad way.

404
26:41.100 --> 26:44.394
I like having autonomy in my research, so that's actually a plus for me.

405
26:44.478 --> 26:46.230
Really? That's good to hear.

406
26:48.440 --> 26:50.067
-Your leg... -Yes?

407
26:50.150 --> 26:51.360
Is your leg okay?

408
26:52.194 --> 26:53.821
No, I'm fine. It's just...

409
26:56.490 --> 26:58.242
I have a prosthetic right leg,

410
26:58.325 --> 27:00.536
so it can be a little inconvenient sometimes.

411
27:01.703 --> 27:04.998
Yeah, I heard you had your leg amputated because of cancer.

412
27:08.919 --> 27:12.464
Even that got around? All the way to Daejeon?

413
27:12.548 --> 27:16.093
Well, I wouldn't say it got around. You're just that famous.

414
27:17.052 --> 27:20.055
Famous for what? For being a disabled researcher?

415
27:20.556 --> 27:22.391
Well, that could be part of it.

416
27:24.393 --> 27:27.855
Ah, I heard you were a competitive swimmer in high school too.

417
27:29.398 --> 27:30.399
Yeah, I guess.

418
27:31.316 --> 27:32.651
You don't swim anymore?

419
27:35.821 --> 27:37.030
No, I don't.

420
27:38.073 --> 27:39.074
Why not?

421
27:40.742 --> 27:43.954
What do you mean, why not? Because I don't want to, obviously.

422
27:45.122 --> 27:48.584
[Sejin] Well, it's still early spring, so the water will probably be cold.

423
27:51.712 --> 27:53.922
Are you always this insensitive?

424
27:57.426 --> 27:59.636
Well, no one's ever called me that before.

425
28:02.598 --> 28:03.599
Ah.

426
28:04.474 --> 28:06.810
Some people do call me nuts, though.

427
28:10.188 --> 28:13.108
This is a prototype robot that's been passed down to us.

428
28:13.191 --> 28:15.235
-You said you were into LEGOs, right? -[Youjin] Yes.

429
28:15.319 --> 28:17.613
Right. Just like the joints on a LEGO model move,

430
28:17.696 --> 28:20.657
these motors let the robot move all its joints.

431
28:20.741 --> 28:21.742
These motors here.

432
28:22.618 --> 28:25.370
The motors... Come this way.

433
28:25.454 --> 28:28.165
-This... Look here.

434
28:28.248 --> 28:31.585
[Hangyeol] Youjin, you haven't seen something like this before, have you?

435
28:31.668 --> 28:33.462
-[Youjin] What? -[Hangyeol] Something like this.

436
28:33.545 --> 28:34.546
What's this?

437
28:34.630 --> 28:36.548
This is what we call a robot hand.

438
28:37.257 --> 28:40.802
It can sense touch and has joints too, just like a human hand.

439
28:41.303 --> 28:43.305
Want to say hi? A handshake?

440
28:44.222 --> 28:45.974
-[Youjin chuckles] -[Taeho in robotic voice] Youjin.

441
28:46.808 --> 28:47.809
Youjin.

442
28:49.019 --> 28:50.395
Nice to meet you.

443
28:52.689 --> 28:54.316
-[in normal voice] Cool, isn't it? -Yeah.

444
28:54.399 --> 28:57.736
Youjin, this is the robot we're making these days.

445
28:57.819 --> 29:01.448
You can come closer and touch it if you want. It's okay.

446
29:02.866 --> 29:04.868
Its name is Danny.

447
29:05.869 --> 29:07.079
As in Daniel Craig.

448
29:07.788 --> 29:10.207
The James Bond actor. You know him, right?

449
29:11.458 --> 29:12.459
Oh.

450
29:13.043 --> 29:14.211
Cool, right?

451
29:16.588 --> 29:19.424
So Danny is a male robot?

452
29:21.510 --> 29:22.511
Yeah, he's male.

453
29:23.637 --> 29:25.263
So, is there a female robot too?

454
29:25.764 --> 29:27.057
Hmm? Uh...

455
29:27.766 --> 29:31.937
Well, I wouldn't say it's male.

456
29:32.020 --> 29:34.773
It's more like... unisex.

457
29:37.275 --> 29:41.238
It can be a man and a woman.

458
29:42.906 --> 29:44.282
[Hangyeol] Oh, like this.

459
29:45.534 --> 29:46.702
-Youjin. -Yes.

460
29:46.785 --> 29:49.663
Hold this bat here. Now, watch me.

461
29:50.247 --> 29:54.251
Stand here and pull it back as far as you can.

462
29:54.334 --> 29:57.754
Bam! See that? This is how you do it.

463
29:58.755 --> 30:01.341
Yeah. Just stand here and bam!

464
30:01.925 --> 30:03.385
Hit it nice and loud.

465
30:03.468 --> 30:06.221
-Like this? -Here, stand in front of it like this.

466
30:07.097 --> 30:09.391
Like this. And this here...

467
30:10.559 --> 30:12.269
-Pull it in like this. -[Youjin] Like this?

468
30:12.352 --> 30:14.396
All right. Then, bam!

469
30:14.479 --> 30:16.898
-It's just a test. -It's a test. Give it a go.

470
30:19.359 --> 30:21.028
Huh? [laughs]

471
30:21.111 --> 30:24.364
No. You can hit it much harder.

472
30:26.241 --> 30:28.577
Uh, but I feel bad for the robot.

473
30:28.660 --> 30:29.661
I mean...

474
30:29.745 --> 30:32.205
No, you don't need to feel bad, Youjin.

475
30:32.289 --> 30:35.042
Imagine it's someone you hate.

476
30:35.125 --> 30:38.336
Think of it as someone you really hate.

477
30:38.920 --> 30:41.089
-Bam! Hit it as hard as you can. -[Hangyeol] Yeah.

478
30:41.173 --> 30:43.759
[Chansoo] You don't need to feel bad for it. It's just a test.

479
30:43.842 --> 30:45.010
[Hangyeol] It's a test.

480
30:45.093 --> 30:47.971
[Taeho] An important test to see how much impact the robot can withstand.

481
30:48.055 --> 30:49.389
-So just... -Bam!

482
30:49.473 --> 30:51.475
-[Taeho] This is a serious test. -[Chansoo] It's a test.

483
30:51.558 --> 30:52.559
[Minjae] But...

484
30:52.642 --> 30:54.269
[Hangyeol] Please take it seriously.

485
30:54.352 --> 30:58.690
...if you like machines and you're good at building with LEGOs,

486
30:59.566 --> 31:01.026
they can be your hobbies.

487
31:01.109 --> 31:02.819
Why go so far as to switch majors?

488
31:03.570 --> 31:05.280
What if you get into grad school,

489
31:05.363 --> 31:08.033
and it turns out that you don't have any talent

490
31:09.117 --> 31:10.619
for mechanical engineering?

491
31:11.453 --> 31:13.538
Are you going to switch to business then?

492
31:16.500 --> 31:19.211
I've got some more work to do at the lab, so I'll get going.

493
31:19.294 --> 31:21.254
Enjoy your meal, and get to know each other.

494
31:21.338 --> 31:22.964
Your matchmaker will leave you to it.

495
31:26.968 --> 31:30.764
-[Miran] Are you lecturing me right now? -[others chattering indistinctly]

496
31:33.016 --> 31:34.851
You're obviously so smart.

497
31:34.935 --> 31:39.606
Who am I to try to guide or teach someone like you?

498
31:42.192 --> 31:43.193
Just go for it!

499
31:44.277 --> 31:45.487
Bam!

500
31:52.869 --> 31:53.870
What was that sound?

501
31:57.999 --> 31:59.918
[groans softly] It's...

502
32:00.836 --> 32:02.587
[yelling] What are you doing?

503
32:05.549 --> 32:06.800
[Chansoo] It's not...

504
32:11.805 --> 32:12.806
[Taeho] We were...

505
32:16.351 --> 32:19.354
Looks like we'll have to end the tour here today. You can go.

506
32:19.437 --> 32:20.438
Okay.

507
32:26.361 --> 32:27.571
-You should leave. -[Taeho] Minjae.

508
32:27.654 --> 32:29.197
-[Minjae] Don't touch that. -[Taeho] It was a test.

509
32:29.281 --> 32:30.532
[Hangyeol] Yeah.

510
32:32.909 --> 32:34.578
[Taeho softly] Come on, let's go.

511
32:35.453 --> 32:36.663
Sorry.

512
33:04.274 --> 33:06.943
-[clicks] -[motor whirring]

513
33:13.658 --> 33:15.327
-[grunts softly] -[motor whirring]

514
33:38.099 --> 33:39.684
-[thuds] -[groans]

515
33:54.866 --> 33:57.202
I can't take this shit anymore! Damn it!

516
34:01.748 --> 34:03.500
-[yelling] -[objects clattering]

517
35:05.353 --> 35:06.855
-[soft whirring] -[latch clicks]

518
35:56.738 --> 36:00.450
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

519
36:01.826 --> 36:03.161
[nurse] Mr. Park Minjae.

520
36:03.244 --> 36:04.245
Yes.

521
36:15.632 --> 36:17.258
-[groans] Doctor. -Yeah.

522
36:17.342 --> 36:19.219
[Minjae] At first, it was only the skin that hurt,

523
36:19.302 --> 36:21.513
so I thought it would go away in a few days.

524
36:22.514 --> 36:25.433
But now it hurts so much I can't even put my prosthetic on.

525
36:25.934 --> 36:27.686
-You've developed an ulcer. -What?

526
36:33.900 --> 36:36.653
But it hasn't even been five months since my last checkup.

527
36:36.736 --> 36:38.405
How did this happen all of a sudden?

528
36:38.488 --> 36:41.366
You've been busy with work, haven't you? And lots of stress?

529
36:41.449 --> 36:43.076
-What? -[doctor] Hardly exercising

530
36:43.159 --> 36:46.538
and eating pizza and fried chicken for dinner every night, right?

531
36:47.038 --> 36:49.666
You've gained 3.8 kg.

532
36:51.626 --> 36:54.087
Jeez, look right here. See? It's pretty obvious.

533
36:55.213 --> 36:59.551
You see, a prosthesis is basically like a piece of clothing made of metal.

534
36:59.634 --> 37:03.722
But unlike a T-shirt or regular clothes, it doesn't stretch.

535
37:05.056 --> 37:08.268
So your body has to fit the prosthesis, not the other way around.

536
37:09.185 --> 37:10.562
Your prosthesis was too tight,

537
37:10.645 --> 37:13.106
which restricted the blood flow and caused the ulcer.

538
37:13.189 --> 37:16.234
So don't worry too much about it, okay?

539
37:18.528 --> 37:19.529
Man.

540
37:20.238 --> 37:21.239
Uh...

541
37:22.240 --> 37:26.995
Wait, so it's not a recurrence or anything like that?

542
37:27.078 --> 37:29.706
That's right. Just keep an eye on your weight.

543
37:31.624 --> 37:34.461
I know you were really worried. Are you disappointed?

544
37:34.544 --> 37:36.755
Doctor, what do you mean, disappointed?

545
37:37.881 --> 37:39.549
I thought it had come back.

546
37:39.632 --> 37:42.010
I cried my eyes out and freaked out.

547
37:42.844 --> 37:44.429
How could I be disappointed?

548
37:44.512 --> 37:46.264
Why would you say it like that?

549
37:47.474 --> 37:49.476
Come on, that's not what I meant.

550
37:50.894 --> 37:53.563
What I'm saying is, an ulcer like this is only superficial.

551
37:53.646 --> 37:57.150
It'll heal quickly, so you don't need to worry.

552
37:58.818 --> 38:00.528
How about getting back into swimming?

553
38:00.612 --> 38:03.114
It's a full-body workout and helps with weight loss.

554
38:03.198 --> 38:06.034
As a former competitive swimmer, you'd know better.

555
38:08.745 --> 38:11.581
Well, I'm not forcing you to do it.

556
38:11.664 --> 38:14.667
But it's a doctor's recommendation, so give it some thought.

557
40:26.883 --> 40:28.509
[staff] We're closing at 10.

558
40:29.844 --> 40:30.845
All right.

559
40:52.325 --> 40:54.535
[Minjae scoffs] 40 million won?

560
40:54.619 --> 40:57.956
[Taeho] Yeah. They said we'll probably need to replace the motor

561
40:58.039 --> 40:59.540
and order a new wrist link.

562
41:01.668 --> 41:04.754
All right, fine. I'll tell the professor myself.

563
41:04.837 --> 41:09.008
Right. Youjin said she sent an email to Professor Ahn.

564
41:09.092 --> 41:10.677
Could you please look into that too?

565
41:10.760 --> 41:11.761
[Minjae] Youjin?

566
41:13.012 --> 41:14.514
Yeah, Lim Youjin.

567
41:14.597 --> 41:16.099
Lim Youjin from the other day.

568
41:18.184 --> 41:20.436
[groans] Just thinking about it pisses me off.

569
41:20.520 --> 41:23.523
What were you guys doing while she caused all that trouble?

570
41:23.606 --> 41:25.274
Why did you just let it happen?

571
41:25.358 --> 41:28.695
Well, we didn't know it'd turn into such a big problem.

572
41:29.445 --> 41:31.072
Turns out she's really strong.

573
41:34.158 --> 41:37.578
But she was pretty shaken up herself.

574
41:37.662 --> 41:41.499
She went white as a sheet and kept apologizing to us. Gosh.

575
41:41.582 --> 41:43.960
It made me feel so bad.

576
41:46.421 --> 41:47.922
Minjae, if we're being honest,

577
41:48.006 --> 41:49.966
what happened in the lab that day was on us.

578
41:50.049 --> 41:52.719
Youjin didn't do anything wrong.

579
41:52.802 --> 41:55.346
She happened to be there at the wrong time.

580
41:55.430 --> 41:57.557
Right? Come on. Right?

581
41:59.434 --> 42:02.186
Well, since things have turned out this way,

582
42:02.270 --> 42:05.148
maybe all this happened for a reason.

583
42:05.231 --> 42:08.359
It'd be great if we could all work together here in the lab--

584
42:08.443 --> 42:09.777
I already filled the spot.

585
42:09.861 --> 42:11.070
-Already? -Yeah.

586
42:11.863 --> 42:12.864
Okay.

587
42:12.947 --> 42:15.116
He's an electrical engineering major at KAIST.

588
42:15.199 --> 42:17.243
His papers and grades are both great.

589
42:17.326 --> 42:20.163
He even did URP in undergrad, so I hired him right away.

590
42:20.246 --> 42:24.542
Hold on, are you talking about Samjin or Sajin or whatever, that KAIST nutjob?

591
42:25.168 --> 42:26.335
He's not a nutjob.

592
42:26.419 --> 42:29.839
Minjae, everyone in KAIST knows he's nuts. Okay?

593
42:29.922 --> 42:32.425
He contacted our school because they all know he's nuts.

594
42:32.508 --> 42:34.719
I don't care. A lot of smart people are nuts.

595
42:34.802 --> 42:38.556
[scoffs] Really? Then I must be nuts too.

596
42:38.639 --> 42:39.640
Are you not?

597
42:48.357 --> 42:49.358
Yes?

598
42:52.862 --> 42:54.572
-Hi. -[Jaehong] Hey, Minjae. Come in.

599
42:57.784 --> 43:00.078
Did you go to the hospital? What did they say?

600
43:00.161 --> 43:02.580
Ah, nothing much.

601
43:02.663 --> 43:05.750
They said I should exercise, lose weight, and take better care of myself.

602
43:05.833 --> 43:06.834
-[Jaehong] Yeah? -Yeah.

603
43:06.918 --> 43:09.629
From the way you're walking, you seem to be doing better.

604
43:09.712 --> 43:11.089
Yeah, I'm doing fine. Yes.

605
43:12.423 --> 43:16.385
I got an email from an interesting student.

606
43:16.469 --> 43:19.097
-[Minjae] Yes. -She's a fashion and textiles graduate,

607
43:19.180 --> 43:21.516
and she wants to study in our program.

608
43:23.392 --> 43:25.478
Apparently, math was her second major.

609
43:26.270 --> 43:28.940
Math is the foundation of algorithm design, after all.

610
43:29.023 --> 43:30.691
-But, Professor, we already... -[line ringing]

611
43:30.775 --> 43:32.527
Yeah. Wait, one second. Sorry.

612
43:33.069 --> 43:35.863
-Hello? Hey, Professor Kang. -[Miran] Hey, Professor Ahn.

613
43:35.947 --> 43:38.199
-Are you busy now? -[Miran] I've got time.

614
43:38.282 --> 43:40.493
-Can you talk for a minute? -[Miran] Yes, sure.

615
43:40.576 --> 43:42.286
I just wanted to ask you something.

616
43:42.370 --> 43:44.705
[Miran] Okay, what is it? Go ahead and ask me now.

617
43:44.789 --> 43:46.999
-Really? Now? -[Miran] Yes.

618
43:47.083 --> 43:48.084
Hmm.

619
43:48.793 --> 43:49.877
Then...

620
43:51.045 --> 43:52.964
How about we meet up and grab a bite?

621
43:53.047 --> 43:56.217
[Miran] I'd be honored. Are you buying?

622
43:57.760 --> 43:59.887
Of course, I should buy. Yeah.

623
43:59.971 --> 44:01.681
[Miran] Then, let's meet at the Faculty Club.

624
44:01.764 --> 44:04.058
-Okay. That's a good choice. Yeah. -[Miran] Yeah.

625
44:04.142 --> 44:06.269
-All right. I'll see you there. -[Miran] See you there.

626
44:06.352 --> 44:08.104
-Okay, bye. -[Miran] Bye.

627
44:09.897 --> 44:11.190
Have you had lunch yet?

628
44:11.274 --> 44:13.693
Sorry? No, I haven't yet.

629
44:14.360 --> 44:15.653
Come with me.

630
44:15.736 --> 44:16.988
FACULTY CLUB

631
44:18.239 --> 44:21.659
There you are.

632
44:22.243 --> 44:23.661
It's been a while.

633
44:24.537 --> 44:27.081
This is my lab assistant.

634
44:27.165 --> 44:28.374
Nice to meet you.

635
44:28.457 --> 44:29.709
I'm Park Minjae.

636
44:29.792 --> 44:30.793
Mm-hmm.

637
44:33.504 --> 44:35.715
Gosh, it's been ages.

638
44:35.798 --> 44:38.342
You only ever call when you need something.

639
44:38.426 --> 44:41.721
Yeah. I'm sorry. I've been too busy.

640
44:41.804 --> 44:43.890
Are you the only busy one here? What about me?

641
44:43.973 --> 44:46.893
I know. That's why I'm treating you to lunch today.

642
44:47.393 --> 44:49.896
-Excuse me. -Hello. Can we have the menu, please?

643
44:51.981 --> 44:52.982
Thank you.

644
45:07.622 --> 45:08.623
Thank you.

645
45:28.851 --> 45:29.852
[Miran] Lim Youjin?

646
45:29.936 --> 45:31.270
-Yeah. -[Miran] Yeah, I know her.

647
45:31.354 --> 45:32.855
She's one of our graduates.

648
45:33.606 --> 45:36.776
But I had no idea she'd contacted the mechanical engineering department.

649
45:36.859 --> 45:41.697
Yeah, I was surprised too. She has a pretty unique background.

650
45:41.781 --> 45:43.783
It's not just her background that's unique.

651
45:43.866 --> 45:46.410
She's pretty unique herself.

652
45:46.494 --> 45:49.330
Yeah? She's unique? Unique how?

653
45:50.373 --> 45:52.792
Well, how should I put it?

654
45:53.668 --> 45:55.670
She's a bright kid. She's smart.

655
45:55.753 --> 45:59.382
Yeah, looks like she did well in undergrad. Her grades are good.

656
45:59.465 --> 46:01.467
But when I say she's smart...

657
46:03.052 --> 46:05.596
You know, kids these days aren't like we were at their age.

658
46:05.680 --> 46:06.681
Ah.

659
46:07.556 --> 46:10.309
She's book-smart,

660
46:10.393 --> 46:13.020
but she's kind of self-centered?

661
46:13.729 --> 46:15.439
[Miran] We're educators ourselves,

662
46:15.523 --> 46:18.359
but something's seriously wrong with the education system.

663
46:18.442 --> 46:20.486
Look how hard we push kids to compete.

664
46:20.569 --> 46:23.948
No one's a friend. Everyone's the enemy. Everything's about competition.

665
46:24.031 --> 46:25.533
"I have to beat everyone."

666
46:25.616 --> 46:27.410
"If I don't crush you, I'm the one who goes down."

667
46:27.493 --> 46:28.494
That's the mentality.

668
46:28.577 --> 46:33.457
Yeah, but that's because we adults failed to teach them better.

669
46:33.541 --> 46:36.377
At the end of the day, they're all victims too. Victims.

670
46:36.460 --> 46:39.463
Yeah, exactly. They're all victims.

671
46:40.548 --> 46:42.049
I feel so bad for them.

672
46:43.050 --> 46:44.885
But as far as I know,

673
46:44.969 --> 46:48.806
she got along fine with her friends.

674
46:49.473 --> 46:51.434
Well, that's what I heard...

675
46:52.268 --> 46:54.228
[Jaehong] You know this student too?

676
46:55.187 --> 46:59.150
I don't know her that well. We just say hi when passing by on campus.

677
46:59.358 --> 47:00.901
You say hi when you pass each other?

678
47:00.985 --> 47:03.070
-You don't know her well? -[Minjae] Right.

679
47:04.322 --> 47:09.702
Do you know the saying, "Biinbujeon Bujaeseungdeok"?

680
47:09.785 --> 47:11.287
Yes, I do.

681
47:12.663 --> 47:15.833
People of poor character should hold no position of authority.

682
47:15.916 --> 47:17.918
Nor should they be taught valuable skills.

683
47:18.419 --> 47:21.922
And that talent and knowledge should never take precedence over virtue.

684
47:22.006 --> 47:24.717
[Jaehong] There's a saying like that? That's a great one.

685
47:25.301 --> 47:28.721
[Miran laughs] There is. God, you engineers are so uncultured.

686
47:28.804 --> 47:30.014
I know, right?

687
47:30.598 --> 47:31.766
Except for you, Mr. Park.

688
47:34.477 --> 47:35.478
Yeah.

689
47:36.228 --> 47:38.939
[Miran] Now that you're pursuing an academic career

690
47:39.023 --> 47:41.525
and will be teaching students yourself,

691
47:42.818 --> 47:44.445
I hope you'll keep that in mind.

692
47:45.529 --> 47:46.530
I will.

693
47:47.615 --> 47:49.408
Well, I should keep it in mind.

694
47:49.492 --> 47:52.411
But who said that? Was it Confucius?

695
47:53.704 --> 47:55.456
You don't need to know.

696
47:55.539 --> 47:57.583
Even if I told you, you'd forget it anyway.

697
47:57.666 --> 47:59.668
Yeah, a hundred percent.

698
48:08.427 --> 48:09.428
-Subin. -[Subin] Yes.

699
48:09.512 --> 48:11.430
-Can I have a cup of green tea? -Sure.

700
48:24.026 --> 48:26.028
-[Subin] Here's your tea. -Yeah. Thanks.

701
48:29.532 --> 48:31.909
Have you been in touch with Youjin lately?

702
48:31.992 --> 48:32.993
Ah...

703
48:33.536 --> 48:35.413
No, I haven't.

704
48:36.122 --> 48:37.123
Yeah?

705
48:37.748 --> 48:40.876
She contacted the mechanical engineering department. Did you know?

706
48:40.960 --> 48:42.169
Mechanical engineering?

707
48:43.295 --> 48:44.296
Uh...

708
48:44.380 --> 48:46.507
Hmm. So you didn't know.

709
48:47.842 --> 48:51.679
You two were so close as undergrads. And you don't even keep in touch now?

710
48:52.888 --> 48:55.433
-We're both really busy, so... -[Miran] Yeah.

711
48:56.016 --> 48:57.518
You're both busy.

712
48:57.601 --> 48:59.687
Friends are only friends when they stay close.

713
48:59.770 --> 49:01.480
Once you drift apart, it's pointless.

714
49:02.565 --> 49:03.566
See?

715
49:03.649 --> 49:08.154
I'm telling you, I'm the only one who looks out for you, Subin.

716
49:26.547 --> 49:27.548
Hello.

717
49:29.049 --> 49:30.468
What brings you here?

718
49:31.552 --> 49:32.553
Uh...

719
49:33.179 --> 49:36.807
I heard he ended up in the hospital after Youjin hit him.

720
49:37.641 --> 49:39.852
Ah, he was hospitalized?

721
49:42.813 --> 49:46.150
He said he'd sue us if we sued him.

722
49:47.234 --> 49:49.862
I was so scared and didn't know what to do.

723
49:50.821 --> 49:53.324
So I told Professor Kang about it, and she helped me.

724
49:53.407 --> 49:55.075
She even paid the hospital bills.

725
49:55.659 --> 49:57.286
So you two were...

726
49:59.288 --> 50:01.665
not dating or anything...

727
50:01.749 --> 50:03.250
[Sujin] No, absolutely not.

728
50:04.919 --> 50:08.005
The professor said we could just go with that and move on

729
50:08.923 --> 50:11.926
since we wouldn't have to see each other again anyway

730
50:12.009 --> 50:14.845
and there was no need to make a bigger deal out of it.

731
50:16.013 --> 50:17.848
So that's what we did.

732
50:18.724 --> 50:19.725
Oh.

733
50:20.726 --> 50:21.810
Honestly,

734
50:22.645 --> 50:26.148
being questioned at the police station wasn't exactly pleasant.

735
50:26.232 --> 50:27.608
It was really scary.

736
50:27.691 --> 50:28.776
But...

737
50:29.735 --> 50:32.655
Lim Youjin didn't seem to know about that.

738
50:35.491 --> 50:38.494
And you two stopped talking to each other.

739
50:41.497 --> 50:42.915
Would that also happen to be

740
50:42.998 --> 50:45.709
because of something Professor Kang Miran said?

741
50:49.004 --> 50:51.090
What is it? What did she say?

742
50:52.049 --> 50:55.970
Youjin wouldn't listen to the professor.

743
50:56.887 --> 51:01.642
And that wasn't all. I heard she even talked back to her.

744
51:02.977 --> 51:03.978
Hmm.

745
51:05.104 --> 51:08.524
Now, no one in our department can talk to Youjin anymore.

746
51:12.611 --> 51:14.280
GRADUATE SCHOOL APPLICATION FORM

747
51:14.363 --> 51:16.991
LIM YOUJIN AHN JAEHONG

748
51:22.663 --> 51:24.957
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY GRADUATE SCHOOL APPLICATION

749
51:25.040 --> 51:26.417
MECHANICAL ENGINEERING

750
51:33.382 --> 51:35.342
YOUR APPLICATION HAS BEEN SUCCESSFULLY SUBMITTED

751
52:49.875 --> 52:50.918
Oh.

752
52:52.002 --> 52:53.003
Hi.

753
53:08.769 --> 53:09.770
[Sejin] Hello.

754
53:09.853 --> 53:12.564
Hi. You can sit wherever you want.

755
53:35.337 --> 53:37.131
-Here. -Thank you.

756
53:51.311 --> 53:54.440
DERIVE THE ROTATION MATRIX FOR ZYX EULER ANGLES

757
53:55.733 --> 53:57.234
Have any of you seen Good Will Hunting?

758
53:58.527 --> 53:59.528
I have.

759
54:00.320 --> 54:01.321
I haven't.

760
54:01.905 --> 54:05.617
It's a movie. The main character's a math genius.

761
54:05.701 --> 54:07.703
If you haven't seen it, make sure you do sometime.

762
54:07.786 --> 54:09.204
It's a classic.

763
54:09.872 --> 54:11.707
And what if you haven't watched it?

764
54:11.790 --> 54:14.168
It has nothing to do with this. It's okay.

765
54:37.691 --> 54:38.734
[Youjin] Excuse me.

766
54:39.777 --> 54:40.778
What is it?

767
54:44.406 --> 54:45.616
You don't know Euler angles?

768
54:46.200 --> 54:49.703
I mean... Do we have to use Euler angles?

769
54:49.786 --> 54:51.163
Oh.

770
54:51.788 --> 54:55.459
Isn't that obvious? You need to solve it the way the question asks.

771
54:56.043 --> 54:57.753
Just do what you can.

772
55:00.589 --> 55:02.341
All right. You may begin.

773
56:31.013 --> 56:33.015
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER

774
57:11.720 --> 57:13.722
Was it a little too difficult?

775
57:13.805 --> 57:14.806
Ah.

776
57:15.432 --> 57:19.353
Well, I just blanked on the harmonic addition theorem.

777
57:19.436 --> 57:20.562
Hmm.

778
57:28.028 --> 57:29.071
Good work.

779
57:34.368 --> 57:37.037
I'm really sorry about what happened that day.

780
57:38.205 --> 57:39.331
Hmm?

781
57:39.414 --> 57:41.500
I know I've got some nerve

782
57:41.583 --> 57:44.670
asking you to let me back into the lab after the huge mess I caused.

783
57:45.629 --> 57:47.255
But please give me one more chance.

784
57:48.674 --> 57:52.678
Seeing the robot in person made me love robotics even more.

785
57:53.345 --> 57:54.638
I really want to study it.

786
57:54.721 --> 57:55.722
Hmm.

787
57:56.682 --> 57:57.683
Okay.

788
57:59.643 --> 58:00.852
Good work today.

789
58:02.562 --> 58:05.148
You said it'd be a waste of four years.

790
58:06.817 --> 58:09.236
But why is that a waste? It was a learning experience.

791
58:11.363 --> 58:13.782
Everyone stumbles and fails sometimes,

792
58:14.825 --> 58:19.329
but I believe we have to learn from it, pick ourselves back up, and keep going.

793
58:23.041 --> 58:24.793
I'm sorry if that was out of line.

794
58:28.296 --> 58:29.297
But...

795
58:30.173 --> 58:33.927
what are you going to do if you fail the test?

796
58:34.428 --> 58:35.762
Then...

797
58:37.347 --> 58:40.267
I'll take another one until I get in.

798
58:41.935 --> 58:42.936
You can go now.

799
58:43.812 --> 58:44.813
Okay.

800
58:59.369 --> 59:02.873
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER LIM YOUJIN

801
59:02.956 --> 59:07.043
She basically wrote a whole thesis here.

802
59:10.464 --> 59:12.591
One is a nutjob,

803
59:12.674 --> 59:16.595
and the other one's got some personality issues.

804
59:16.678 --> 59:18.263
-[Minjae] Oh... -A nutjob would be better, right?

805
59:18.764 --> 59:22.350
I mean, our research involves a lot of teamwork.

806
59:26.021 --> 59:27.731
Well,

807
59:27.814 --> 59:31.401
she can be pretty stubborn and a little eccentric,

808
59:31.985 --> 59:36.198
but she definitely doesn't have any serious character issues.

809
59:38.074 --> 59:41.703
And from what I've seen, she seems very determined to study.

810
59:43.246 --> 59:47.501
Unless there are any major concerns about her abilities,

811
59:47.584 --> 59:52.172
I personally think we'd be fine admitting her...

812
59:55.008 --> 59:57.344
She wrote so tiny I can barely even read it.

813
59:58.136 --> 01:00:02.349
Or maybe we should just show this to Professor Lee.

814
01:00:02.432 --> 01:00:03.642
That could work.

815
01:00:05.101 --> 01:00:07.103
I wonder if Professor Lee is in his office.

816
01:00:08.897 --> 01:00:11.608
[Jaehong] How was your first semester teaching Korean students

817
01:00:11.691 --> 01:00:13.568
after teaching in the US?

818
01:00:13.652 --> 01:00:15.821
Well, we have a very different talent pool here.

819
01:00:15.904 --> 01:00:17.906
Yeah, that's true,

820
01:00:17.989 --> 01:00:19.825
but we have plenty of talented students too.

821
01:00:19.908 --> 01:00:20.909
Right.

822
01:00:20.992 --> 01:00:23.119
[Jaehong] It all depends on the teacher, though.

823
01:00:24.788 --> 01:00:27.290
Still, it's good to be back in Korea, right?

824
01:00:28.041 --> 01:00:31.253
I mean, the food is great here.

825
01:00:33.338 --> 01:00:34.422
Yeah, that's true.

826
01:00:38.468 --> 01:00:40.053
-Is this a female student? -Hmm?

827
01:00:40.929 --> 01:00:41.930
Yes.

828
01:00:42.013 --> 01:00:43.014
Hmm...

829
01:00:44.808 --> 01:00:46.893
-It's good. -It's good?

830
01:00:46.977 --> 01:00:48.520
I can tell she's got talent.

831
01:00:49.062 --> 01:00:51.273
But why does she want to study mechanical engineering?

832
01:00:51.356 --> 01:00:54.776
Well, because machines are more fun than math, obviously.

833
01:00:55.277 --> 01:00:58.071
Ah, she can join the math program. We'll take her.

834
01:00:58.154 --> 01:01:00.615
We can't do that. We need more students too.

835
01:01:00.699 --> 01:01:02.784
-Yes. -Right? It's serious.

836
01:01:02.868 --> 01:01:06.538
Well, she said she wanted to study mechanical engineering, so...

837
01:01:06.621 --> 01:01:10.917
Exactly. We should respect what she wants to do.

838
01:01:11.001 --> 01:01:13.420
Tell her to contact our department, just in case.

839
01:01:13.503 --> 01:01:16.298
Come on, I said we can't. Stop trying to steal our student.

840
01:01:16.381 --> 01:01:18.383
-Just in case. -No way.

841
01:01:19.968 --> 01:01:21.136
Don't even think about it.

842
01:01:22.971 --> 01:01:24.598
He's really hard to impress.

843
01:01:24.681 --> 01:01:26.308
If even he's saying that,

844
01:01:27.183 --> 01:01:28.935
she must be a real genius.

845
01:01:29.019 --> 01:01:30.228
-Watch out. -It's okay.

846
01:01:32.397 --> 01:01:34.357
I don't know if she's a genius...

847
01:01:34.441 --> 01:01:36.026
-You know, Minjae. -Yes.

848
01:01:36.109 --> 01:01:38.445
You really do have a good eye for people.

849
01:01:38.528 --> 01:01:39.529
Not at all.

850
01:01:41.197 --> 01:01:44.701
I guess this could be a good chance for us to prepare for the WRS.

851
01:01:45.952 --> 01:01:48.788
I heard they're already preparing for it at KAIST.

852
01:01:48.872 --> 01:01:52.083
Really? If they can do it, there's no way we can't.

853
01:01:52.751 --> 01:01:54.169
-Right. -Oh, man.

854
01:01:54.252 --> 01:01:58.298
My heart's racing just thinking about crushing them this time.

855
01:02:01.134 --> 01:02:04.971
So, what are we going to do with Lim Youjin?

856
01:02:05.055 --> 01:02:06.348
Are we admitting her?

857
01:02:07.140 --> 01:02:09.351
Why would a genius get rejected from grad school?

858
01:02:09.434 --> 01:02:11.311
What are you even talking about?

859
01:02:13.772 --> 01:02:15.190
-[Youseong] Mmm. [slurps] -[Youjin screams]

860
01:02:15.273 --> 01:02:16.942
-[Youseong] This is good. -[door opens]

861
01:02:17.025 --> 01:02:18.360
-What's going on? -[footsteps approaching]

862
01:02:18.443 --> 01:02:19.444
-What is it? -[Youjin] Mom!

863
01:02:19.527 --> 01:02:20.654
[Youseong] It's seasoned perfectly.

864
01:02:20.737 --> 01:02:21.905
-[Youjin] I got in. -What?

865
01:02:21.988 --> 01:02:24.032
I got it. I got in!

866
01:02:24.115 --> 01:02:26.785
-Oh, my God! Well done, Youjin! -I got into grad school!

867
01:02:26.868 --> 01:02:29.120
[Miyoung] Well done!

868
01:02:29.204 --> 01:02:31.623
My girl, well done!

869
01:02:32.123 --> 01:02:34.542
If she studied that much and still didn't get in,

870
01:02:34.626 --> 01:02:36.628
she'd be worse than an idiot.

871
01:02:38.922 --> 01:02:42.717
You did a great job. That's my girl. Well done!

872
01:03:17.419 --> 01:03:18.753
-[Hangyeol] She's here. -[Taeho] Hmm?

873
01:03:18.837 --> 01:03:20.338
-I'm sorry I'm late. -[Taeho] Hey!

874
01:03:20.422 --> 01:03:22.674
No, you're not late.

875
01:03:22.757 --> 01:03:25.760
Let's see. See? You came right on time.

876
01:03:25.844 --> 01:03:28.221
As your junior, I should've come earlier and waited.

877
01:03:28.304 --> 01:03:31.725
Well, I appreciate your respect for seniority.

878
01:03:32.892 --> 01:03:34.519
You can drop the formalities with me.

879
01:03:36.354 --> 01:03:37.731
Can I really do that?

880
01:03:40.775 --> 01:03:44.779
[hesitates] Okay, then. Youjin.

881
01:03:47.449 --> 01:03:49.617
-Does that go for me too? -Sure.

882
01:03:49.701 --> 01:03:52.746
-Then I guess I'll do the same. -Of course.

883
01:03:54.039 --> 01:03:56.458
You're really easygoing.

884
01:03:57.417 --> 01:03:58.960
When is Minjae going to join us?

885
01:03:59.044 --> 01:04:02.213
-Hold on. -Minjae is coming with Chacha.

886
01:04:02.297 --> 01:04:03.798
-[Taeho] Yeah. -Chacha?

887
01:04:06.217 --> 01:04:10.889
I'm sure you've met her once. You know, at the GN Electronics office.

888
01:04:11.473 --> 01:04:13.141
Ah, Ms. Cha?

889
01:04:13.224 --> 01:04:15.435
She used to be in our lab.

890
01:04:16.102 --> 01:04:17.103
Yeah, I know.

891
01:04:17.187 --> 01:04:20.106
They're just around the corner. Should we go ahead and order?

892
01:04:23.109 --> 01:04:24.110
[Hangyeol] There they come.

893
01:04:24.736 --> 01:04:25.820
-[Taeho] Huh? Yeah. -[Hangyeol] Hey.

894
01:04:27.489 --> 01:04:29.199
[Seohyun] Traffic is awful around here.

895
01:04:31.117 --> 01:04:32.285
[Seohyun] Oh.

896
01:04:32.368 --> 01:04:33.620
Hello.

897
01:04:34.662 --> 01:04:37.999
-[Minjae] Why haven't you ordered yet? -Well... What should we order?

898
01:04:38.750 --> 01:04:40.376
[Minjae] Oh, no. Hey.

899
01:04:41.044 --> 01:04:42.462
-[Taeho] All right. -[bottle clinking]

900
01:04:44.214 --> 01:04:49.177
Let's welcome our newest lab member, Lim Youjin.

901
01:04:49.260 --> 01:04:50.762
Give her a hand!

902
01:04:54.432 --> 01:04:55.767
Now,

903
01:04:55.850 --> 01:04:59.896
let's hear a few words from Youjin.

904
01:05:05.735 --> 01:05:09.989
Hmm, I... I mean, although I'm from a different major,

905
01:05:10.073 --> 01:05:13.618
uh, and I don't know a lot about robotics research,

906
01:05:14.494 --> 01:05:19.332
I'll work hard and make sure I pull my weight as part of the team.

907
01:05:23.670 --> 01:05:25.380
Wait a minute.

908
01:05:25.880 --> 01:05:28.133
You can't sit down just yet.

909
01:05:29.801 --> 01:05:32.428
Please sing a song.

910
01:05:32.929 --> 01:05:34.389
I can't sing. No, I can't sing.

911
01:05:34.472 --> 01:05:38.059
[chanting] Sing! Sing!

912
01:05:38.143 --> 01:05:42.355
-Sing! Sing! -Sing! Sing!

913
01:06:39.746 --> 01:06:41.873
You guys are in trouble now.

914
01:06:41.956 --> 01:06:44.417
Your newbie is quite a character.

915
01:06:48.171 --> 01:06:49.297
-[customer gasps] -[Seohyun gasps]

916
01:06:49.380 --> 01:06:50.757
[Hangyeol] Hey, Youjin.

917
01:06:50.840 --> 01:06:51.841
Youjin!

918
01:06:52.342 --> 01:06:53.343
Excuse me!

919
01:06:59.974 --> 01:07:03.645
Please send us your messages

920
01:07:03.728 --> 01:07:06.814
online or by text at 93001.

921
01:07:18.326 --> 01:07:20.370
-[Youjin] Hmm... -[softly] Her snore...

922
01:07:42.350 --> 01:07:43.351
Thank you.

923
01:08:02.662 --> 01:08:05.748
So, where do you live?

924
01:08:05.832 --> 01:08:07.625
I'll take you home.

925
01:08:07.709 --> 01:08:08.710
Mmm.

926
01:08:08.793 --> 01:08:11.004
No, it's okay. I can go home by myself.

927
01:08:11.963 --> 01:08:13.381
You're not going home alone.

928
01:08:14.632 --> 01:08:16.217
Come on, where do you live?

929
01:08:16.301 --> 01:08:19.387
No, really. I'm completely sober now.

930
01:08:20.555 --> 01:08:22.390
-Good night, then. -But...

931
01:08:25.601 --> 01:08:27.020
Be careful.

932
01:08:29.063 --> 01:08:30.064
Oh, my God.

933
01:08:31.566 --> 01:08:32.567
Your bag.

934
01:08:33.276 --> 01:08:35.111
You forgot your bag. [groans]

935
01:08:37.322 --> 01:08:38.698
Take your hand out. Like this.

936
01:08:38.781 --> 01:08:40.199
-Huh? -Your bag.

937
01:08:42.285 --> 01:08:44.162
[Youjin] Thank you. Bye.

938
01:08:48.166 --> 01:08:49.417
-[thuds] -Ah.

939
01:08:52.587 --> 01:08:56.257
Okay, fine. Come here. Come this way.

940
01:09:02.263 --> 01:09:03.264
Here.

941
01:09:04.015 --> 01:09:06.934
Sit here and sober up a little before you head home.

942
01:09:09.187 --> 01:09:12.273
Actually, wait. Just stay right here.

943
01:09:26.329 --> 01:09:27.330
I'll just have this.

944
01:09:27.413 --> 01:09:29.207
-[staff] All right. -[scanner beeps]

945
01:09:29.791 --> 01:09:31.918
-Okay, insert your card. -Okay.

946
01:09:35.463 --> 01:09:37.256
-[staff] You're all set. -Thank you.

947
01:10:26.889 --> 01:10:28.891
-[pants] -[meowing]

948
01:10:39.652 --> 01:10:40.653
Oh, boy.

949
01:10:41.821 --> 01:10:44.907
What are you doing here?

950
01:10:45.950 --> 01:10:48.286
It's cold out here. Why did you leave your bag?

951
01:10:50.288 --> 01:10:51.289
Drink this.

952
01:10:59.046 --> 01:11:00.715
If you don't want this, tell me now.

953
01:11:03.468 --> 01:11:04.469
Five.

954
01:11:05.595 --> 01:11:06.596
Four.

955
01:11:08.222 --> 01:11:09.223
Three.

956
01:11:10.683 --> 01:11:11.684
Two.

957
01:11:13.686 --> 01:11:14.687
One.

958
01:12:02.985 --> 01:12:06.906
BETWEEN STEPS

959
01:12:06.989 --> 01:12:07.990
Hi.

960
01:12:08.074 --> 01:12:11.077
It's not like I have a lot of dating experience,

961
01:12:11.160 --> 01:12:12.537
so I'm not sure.

962
01:12:12.620 --> 01:12:14.455
I was pretty drunk that day too.

963
01:12:14.539 --> 01:12:17.625
-[Sejin] Are those two a couple? -[Taeho] High school sweethearts.

964
01:12:17.708 --> 01:12:19.752
-Please, just one picture with this. -No.

965
01:12:19.836 --> 01:12:21.838
When did I disrespect you?

966
01:12:21.921 --> 01:12:24.549
[Subin] The lab assistant is that guy from earlier, right?

967
01:12:24.632 --> 01:12:27.385
[Minjae] Do you want some ice cream? What flavor do you like?

968
01:12:27.468 --> 01:12:28.928
She's not even that pretty.

969
01:12:29.011 --> 01:12:30.596
[Youjin] A goddess. A genius goddess.

970
01:12:30.680 --> 01:12:32.807
[laughing] You're really cute.
